From e18424ddd83310fb66def0d3fa68aff7332a039c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:12:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: keep radio config out of the MLD configuration

wpad decides whether to keep or tear down an MLD interface by comparing the
whole configuration object, which embedded the full device configuration of
every participating radio. Any radio level change, such as a channel or
txpower update, therefore destroyed and recreated the station MLD and
dropped the backhaul link. Neither hostapd nor wpa_supplicant reads
radio_config; it is only used locally to resolve the phy.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

Backported from OpenWrt main: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/commit/e18424ddd83310fb66def0d3fa68aff7332a039c
On 25.12 a txpower or channel change on one radio of an AP MLD left only that
radio's link up: hostapd recreated the MLD, spliced the MLD BSS out of the
other radios, and netifd never reconfigured them because their config was
unchanged.
---
 .../network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless.uc  | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless.uc b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless.uc
index d26e4efbcd..17327213b8 100644
--- a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless.uc
+++ b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless.uc
@@ -29,7 +29,9 @@ function wpad_update_mlo(service, mode)
 		if (!data.phy)
 			continue;
 
-		config[ifname] = data;
+		let entry = { ...data };
+		delete entry.radio_config;
+		config[ifname] = entry;
 	}
 
 	ubus.call({
